:: Fishing Forest Lake Reel
<<effects>>
<<set $fishingReelAttempts += 1>>
<<if $athleticsSuccess>>
	You brace against the rocks and heave, and you <<if $fishingReelAttempts gt 1>>finally<</if>> <span class="green">reel up the fish.</span><<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<br><br>

	<<include "Fishing Forest Lake Catch">>
<<elseif $fishingReelAttempts gte 3 and random(1, 5) gte 4>>
	<<if $rng gte 80>>
		<<fishingForestLakePulledIn>>
	<<elseif $rng gte 60>>
		<<fishingForestLakeRodLost>>
	<<else>>
		<<fishingForestLakeLineSnapped>>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if $fishingReelAttempts is 1>>
		You haul back on your rod, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> strips your line right back off the reel. Your arms burn with the effort.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<<else>>
		You drag it closer, close enough to see its shape beneath the surface, before it dives again, nearly pulling you off the rocks.<<gtiredness>><<tiredness 1>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>

	<<set _reelDifficultyMax to Math.clamp($fishingHookedFish.size * 10, 600, 1400)>>
	<<link [[Keep fighting it|Fishing Forest Lake Reel]]>><</link>><<athleticsdifficulty -250 _reelDifficultyMax>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cut the line|Fishing Forest Lake Cut Line]]>><</link>>
<</if>>


:: Fishing Forest Lake Cut Line
<<effects>>
You release the tension on your rod, letting your line go slack. The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, your line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>


:: Widgets Fishing Forest Lake Catch [widget]
<<widget "fishingForestLakePulledIn">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> pulls harder. <span class="red">Your feet slip on the wet rock and it drags you headfirst into the lake,</span> your rod torn from your hands as you go under.<<gstress>><<stress 4>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Next|Lake Depths]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingForestLakeRodLost">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but the <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> gives one last violent pull and your rod is wrenched clean out of your hands, vanishing into the dark water.<<gstress>><<stress 3>><<handheldruined>>
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Return to fishing|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "fishingForestLakeLineSnapped">>
	You lean back with everything you have left, but your line goes taut, then <span class="red">snaps.</span> The <<print $fishingHookedFish.type>> is gone, and your line goes slack.
	<<unset $fishingHookedFish>>
	<<run stopFishingProp()>>
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Re-hook the line and cast back out (0:03)|Fishing Forest Lake Wait]]>><<pass 3>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave|Lake Fishing Rock]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<</widget>>

:: Fishing Forest Lake Catch
<<effects>>
<<run updateFishRecord($fishingHookedFish.type, $fishingHookedFish.size, $bus)>>
<<run stopFishingProp()>>
<<set _fishPropName to "caught-" + $fishingHookedFish.type>>
<<wearProp _fishPropName>>
<<set _canEatFish to canEatFishTf($fishingHookedFish)>>

<<fishingCatchFishText $fishingHookedFish>>
<br><br>

<<if _canEatFish>>
	It's such a small fish, you could probably fit the whole thing in your mouth.
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<link [[Stow it away|Fishing Forest Lake Keep]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [["Throw the " + $fishingHookedFish.type + " back"|Fishing Forest Lake Throw Back]]>><</link>>
<<if _canEatFish>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Eat the fish|Fishing Forest Lake Cat Eat]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
